      "q": "Which SkyTrain lines serve Burnaby?",
      "a": "Two — the Expo Line connects downtown Vancouver with Burnaby, New Westminster and Surrey (Burnaby stops include Patterson, Metrotown, Royal Oak and Edmonds), and the Millennium Line runs through Burnaby (Brentwood Town Centre, Holdom, Sperling–Burnaby Lake, Lake City Way, Production Way–University, Lougheed Town Centre) into Port Moody and Coquitlam.",
      "gen": "muse"
    },
    {
      "q": "How many units can a Burnaby house lot hold?",
      "a": "In the R1 SSMUH District, up to 3 to 6 dwelling units depending on lot area and proximity to a frequent transit network bus stop, with secondary suites counted inside the total; forms include single-family homes, laneway homes, suites, duplexes, triplexes, fourplexes and, on some properties, fiveplexes and sixplexes.",
      "gen": "muse"
    },
    {
      "q": "What is the Burnaby 2050 OCP?",
